#
# Security region: cpu, locked
#
# sec_cpu_hardened, and the processor-side settings a machine that does one
# job runs at their strongest whether the part says it needs them or not. See
# sec_cpu_hardened for the region.
#
# What it costs is the machine's second thread of every core (mitigations=
# auto,nosmt: a sibling thread is the channel several of the attacks use, and
# the mitigations that close it are partial), the kernel unmapped from every
# user address space even on a part that is not vulnerable to Meltdown
# (pti=on), and the buffer-clearing instructions on every return to user mode
# on a part that has them. A kiosk is rarely at its core count.
#
#> includes sec_cpu_hardened

#> cmdline mitigations=auto,nosmt pti=on tsx=off
